      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime, we need to first identify these prime numbers and then calculate their sum.\n\nThe first six prime numbers are:\n\\[ 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of these first six prime numbers:\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 + 13\n\\]\n\nNow, let's do the addition step-by-step:\n\\[\n2 + 3 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n5 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\\[\n10 + 7 = 17\n\\]\n\\[\n17 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n28 + 13 = 41\n\\]\n\nSo, the sum of the first five prime numbers is 41.\n\nThe sixth prime number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 41 is divided by 13. We perform the division:\n\\[\n41 \\div 13\n\\]\n\nPerforming the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{41}{13} \\approx 3.15 \\quad (\\text{rounded to two decimal places})\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder in simple terms. We start with 41 and subtract multiples of 13 until we get under 13.\n\nStarting with the closest multiple of 13 to 41:\n\\[\n41 - 13 = 28 \\quad (\\text{too large})\n\\]\n\nNext:\n\\[\n28 - 13 = 15 \\quad (\\text{too large})\n\\]\n\nThen:\n\\[\n15 - 13 = 2 \\quad (\\text{within range})\n\\]\n\nFinalize the calculation:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
