      "text": "To solve this problem, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first five primes.\n3. Divide the sum by the sixth prime number.\n4. Find the remainder of the division.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the first six prime numbers\nPrime numbers are those numbers greater than 1 that have no divisors other than 1 and themselves:\n\\[2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the sum of the first five primes\n\\[2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11\\]\n\nLet's compute this sum using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Step 3: Divide the sum by the sixth prime number\nOnce we have the sum, we'll divide it by the sixth prime number (13), and find the remainder.\n\n### Step 4: Find the remainder\n\nLet's execute the Python code to perform these calculations.\n```python\n# First six prime numbers\nprimes = [2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13]\n\n# Sum of the first five primes\nsum_of_primes = sum(primes[:5])\n\n# Sixth prime number\nsixth_prime = primes[5]\n\n# Remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime number\nremainder = sum_of_primes % sixth_prime\n\nprint((sum_of_primes, sixth_prime, remainder))\n```\n```output\n(28, 13, 2)\n```\nThe sum of the first five primes (2, 3, 5, 7, 11) is \\(28\\). When we divide \\(28\\) by the sixth prime number (13), we get a remainder of \\(2\\).\n\nThus, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
